 provides devices and report on the findings. 2. What are the differential diagnoses? (10 marks)","type":"OSCE / Practical Station","subject":"Ophthalmology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Ophthalmology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-18a087a8bf49","stem":"MD3 RADIOLOGY STATION 11 (7 MINUTES) A 14 years old girl presents with pain and swelling in the distal third of the left thigh. The radiographs of the thigh was done. 1. List down 3 (three) important radiological changes seen on the radiograph. MARKS a) _____________________________________________________ 1 b) _____________________________________________________ 1 c) _____________________________________________________ 1 2. What is the most likely diagnosis? a) ______________________________________________________ 1 3. What additional radiological investigation, if any, is/are required to make a treatment decision? a) ______________________________________________________ 1","type":"OSCE / Practical Station","subject":"Radiography and Medical Imaging","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Check list (station 11) III"},{"label":"B","text":"a) Cortical destruction. b) Soft tissue mass. c) Subperiosteal new bone formation. d) Osteoid material in soft tissue/Sun rays or Sun burst appearance/ Soft tissue matrix. e) Pathological fracture"},{"label":"C","text":"a) Osteogenic sarcoma"},{"label":"D","text":"a) Chest X-ray"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Radiography and Medical Imaging","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["possible_multiple_questions_in_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-4a3d27962e0c","stem":"MD3 RADIOLOGY STATION 12 (7 MINUTES) A 25 years old female presents with a history of failure to conceive for two years. A contrast study under fluoroscopy was done on her as seen on the radiographs. MARKS 1. What was the specific investigation done? a) _______________________________________________________ 1 2. What are the two possible indications for the investigation? a) _______________________________________________________ 1 b) _______________________________________________________ 1 3. List down two findings seen on the radiograph. a) _______________________________________________________ 1 b) _______________________________________________________ 1","type":"OSCE / Practical Station","subject":"Radiography and Medical Imaging","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Checklist (station 12) IV"},{"label":"B","text":"a) Hysterosalpingography"},{"label":"C","text":"a) Tube patency b) Morphology of the uterus"},{"label":"D","text":"a) Bilateral tubal spillage b) Normal uterus"},{"label":"E","text":"MD III CLINICAL LAB. STATION 18 (7 MINUTES) Given a gram stained smear Please report your findings Mention the media used to isolate the organism"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Radiography and Medical Imaging","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["possible_multiple_questions_in_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-1edae34a472d",