tted at Mawenzi regional hospital on 25/11/2010 at 5am. Membranes ruptured 2 hours before admission, on the way to hospital. At time of admission FHR 120/min, clear liquor, no moulding. Cervix was dilated 2cm and head was 4/5 she had 3 contraction in 10 minute each last up to 20 seconds. BP was 110/80mmHg, temp. Was 36 C she pass urine 200mls, no acetone, no protein, PR was 80/min. At 9am Cervix was 5cm dilated, head 3/5 FHR 140/minute, clear liquor no moulding she had 4 contraction in 10min each last 20 – 40 seconds, Bp 110/70mmHg. PR 76min ,temp 37 C, she pass urine volume 125mls. At 1pm, Cervix was 10cm dilated, head 1/5 ,clear liquor, no caput. She had 5 contractions in 10minutes, each last more than 40 seconds, FHR was 130/min BP 110/70mmHg, PR 76/mm Temp. 37°C QNS. 1. Plot partograph","type":"Short Answer","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-28b86d16ac9a","stem":"Interpret [Slide 7] PARTOGRAPH cont.. 6; Mrs. Mohamedi was admitted at 8.00am cervix was 3cm dilated, head 4/5. At 12a.m cervix was 6cm dilated head 3/5 .At 4pm head was 3cm and Cervix 7cm. QNS a. Plot patograph and interpret.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"General Surgery","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"General Surgery","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draf