,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-5e1596de4d86","stem":"<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\" standalone=\"no\"?>","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"<ds:datastoreItem ds:itemID=\"{55AF091B-3C7A-41E3-B477-F2FDAA23CFDA}\" xmlns:ds=\"http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/customXml\"><ds:schemaRefs><ds:schemaRef ds:uri=\"http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/2006/coverPageProps\"/><\/ds:schemaRefs><\/ds:datastoreItem>"},{"label":"B","text":"<b:Sources SelectedStyle=\"\\APA.XSL\" StyleName=\"APA\" xmlns:b=\"http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/bibliography\" xmlns=\"http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/bibliography\"><\/b:Sources>"}],"priority":1,"status":"review","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic","mcq_missing_options"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["mcq_missing_options","not_enough_options","prior_structural_review_flag","repeated_question_stem","subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"d33ae42eb5fb87296742a93c0cf6b817f4bfbea4"},{"id":"q-235509a2e62a","stem":"<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\" standalone=\"no\"?>","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"<ds:datastoreItem ds:itemID=\"{07A95660-197C-40F0-B280-E3A0EE612F20}\" xmlns:ds=\"http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/customXml\"><ds:schemaRefs><ds:schemaRef ds:uri=\"http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/bibliography\"/><\/ds:schemaRefs><\/ds:datastoreItem>"},{"label":"B","text":"Microsoft Office Word 97-2003 Document"},{"label":"C","text":"MSWordDoc"},{"label":"D","text":"Word.Document.8"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"d33ae42eb5fb87296742a93c0cf6b817f4bfbea4"},{"id":"q-8b9ab467a00d","stem":"Fibroids ______ Undergoes cancerous transformation in 30% of cases if not treated ______ May lead to iron deficiency anemia ______ Shrinks after menopause and may re-grow following hormonal therapy. ______ May enlarge during pregnancy and then shrinks during the puerperium. ______ Have been reported to cause secondary polycythermia in some few cases Regarding septic abortion the following statement are true","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Obstetrics and Gynecology","topic":"Antenatal Care · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Antenatal Care","options":[{"label":"A","text":"__________The most common infecting organisms are Streptococcus aureus, coliform bacteria, bacteriodes, clostridium welchii."},{"label":"B","text":"__________The most dangerous are the GRAM-POSITIVE & ANAEROBIC organisms which produces endotoxic shock."},{"label":"C","text":"___________Clostridium welchii and Bacteroides necrophorus may cause septic shock."},{"label":"D","text":"___________Mental disorientation and joints pain are among the clinical features"},{"label":"E","text":"____________Curettage should be done as soon as possible"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Obstetrics and Gynecology","displayTopic":"Antenatal Care · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-f43ad68038eb","stem":"Regarding Post Abortion Care","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"_______Unsafe abortion accounts for 25% of maternal deaths worldwide and as much as 13% in some countries"},{"label":"B","text":"_________ For every woman who dies from unsafe abortion, 10 women suffer morbidity"},{"label":"C","text":"__________According to Unicef, unsafe abortions cause 12 percent of deaths among pregnant women in Africa, 6 percent in Asia and 4 percent in Latin America and the Caribbean. . d.___________Community and Service Provider Partnerships helps in creating an awareness."},{"label":"E","text":"___________Counseling is a vital element of care that moves PAC services from more curative to more preventive SECTION C: MATCHING ITEMS QUESTIONS (Total 20 MARKS) Fill in the blank space in column A the letter corresponding in column B Regarding Maternal nutrition Column A Column B I) _________.Risk for folate deficiency A. Strengthening fetal bones II)__________Iron and Iodine B. Formation of blood III)_________Calcium &Vit.D C. Needed in large amount IV)_______Zinc deficiency D. Can cause birth defects in high doses V)_________Vit.A E. Preterm delivery"},{"label":"F","text":"Essential for normal infant brain development"},{"label":"G","text":"Taking phenytoin"},{"label":"H","text":"Cell metabolism and structural growth Fill in the blank space in column A the letter corresponding to the specific clinical feature of the condition in column B Column A Column B I)._____ Higoumenakis sign A. Symmetrical joint swelling II)______ saber shin B. Sharp anterior bowing of the tibia, III)______Clutton's joints C. Enlargement of the sternal end of the right clavicle IV)_______Hutchinson teeth D. Congenital syphilis V)______ Saddle nose"},{"label":"E","text":"Blunted upper incisors"},{"label":"F","text":"Chorioretinitis"},{"label":"G","text":"8th Nerve hearing defect Fill in the blank space in column A the letter corresponding in column B Regarding Septic abortion Column A Column B I)Partially caused by ischaemia and hypotension A. Renal function test II)Infection occurs at 48 hours B.Oliguria III)E.coli and Proteus vulgaris C.Septic abortion IV)Streptococcus aureus & Coliform bacteria D.Septicemia V)Clostridium welchii & Bacteroides necrophorus E.Renal failure"},{"label":"F","text":"Most common infective organisms"},{"label":"G","text":"Can operate even they are dead"},{"label":"H","text":"Septic shock"}],"priority":1,"status":"review","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic","too_many_options_possible_merge","duplicate_option_labels"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["duplicate_option_labels","long_option_manual_review","nonunique_option_labels","prior_structural_review_flag","subject_needs_classification","subject_unclassified","too_many_options","too_many_options_possible_merge","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-0d492c7e0671","stem":"Fill in blank space in column A the letter corresponding to the action in column B I). __________ Day 1: A. Early miscarriage","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"Cleavage, Compaction II)________ Day 3: C. Implantation III)________ Day 5: D. Inner Cell Mass-forms embryo, Trophoblasts-form placenta"},{"label":"E","text":"Cavitation IV)._________ Day 6: .F. Ectopic implantation V)._________Failure implantation G. Normal pregnancy SECTION D SHORT ANSWER & ASSAY QUESTIONS (Total 20 MARKS) Clinically differentiate between septic abortion and missed abortion.( 5 Marks) Worldwide,Asia has the highest absolute number of unsafe abortions and Africa has the highest deathrate from unsafe abortion. DISCUSS. (5marks) Mention four ovarian causes of precocious puberty. (4 marks) Women are physiologically more susceptible to acquiring HIV during unprotected sex than men because (3marks) Mention the WHO Criteria for Diagnosis of Congenital Rubella.(3marks) --------- BEST WISHES-----------"}],"priority":1,"status":"review","flags":["topic_generic","mcq_missing_options"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["long_option_manual_review","mcq_missing_options","not_enough_options","prior_structural_review_flag","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-28f6b3aa1b32","stem":"When operating on the uterus it is important to know that","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Obstetrics and Gynecology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Obstetrics and Gynecology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-9153bcb888af","stem":"What is the most likely diagnosis of a 25 year old woman presenting with secondary amenorrhoea, breast atrophy and deepening of voice.","type":"Short Answer","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-415b64c61e5a","stem":"What is the condition of the patient with abnormal menstrual pattern associated with short follicular phase","type":"Clinical Vignette","subject":"Obstetrics and Gynecology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Obstetrics and Gynecology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-63f9e1c6ce5e","stem":"Which of the following conditions is more likely to present with primary amenorrhoea, recurrent pain and pelvis mass that gets worse during menstrual periods","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Pelvis and Perineum","topicOriginal":"Pelvis and Perineum","subtopic":"Pelvi","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Pelvis and Perineum","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-f3ff99c6ee27","stem":"The Expected date of delivery of a human pregnancy can be calculated","type":"Calculation","subject":"Obstetrics and Gynecology","topic":"Antenatal Care · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Antenatal Care","options":[{"label":"A","text":"From a change in the patient's weight."},{"label":"B","text":"As 10 lunar months after the time of ovulation."},{"label":"C","text":"As 40 weeks after last menstrual period."},{"label":"D","text":"As 280 days from the last full moon."},{"label":"E","text":"As 36 weeks after the last menstrual period."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Obstetrics and Gynecology","displayTopic":"Antenatal Care · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-ccc21f8defb3","stem":"The last menstrual period was June 30. the expected date of delivery (EDD) is approximately","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Obstetrics and Gynecology","topic":"Labor and Delivery · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Labor and Delivery","options":[{"label":"A","text":"March 23."},{"label":"B","text":"April 7."},{"label":"C","text":"March 28."},{"label":"D","text":"April 23."},{"label":"E","text":"March 7. 5 All OB-GYN MCQs Second rearranged Edition 2011 Anatomy of the female genital tract, bony pelvis and fetal skull:"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Obstetrics and Gynecology","displayTopic":"Labor and Delivery · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-c24b15d73ef9","stem":"Uterine Cervix","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Is the portion of the uterus below the isthmus"},{"label":"B","text":"External OS cell lining is columnar epithelium"},{"label":"C","text":"Laterally is attached to the round ligament"},{"label":"D","text":"The cervical canal is covered with stratified squamous epithelium"},{"label":"E","text":"Can be dilated with dilators without the need of anesthesia"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["short_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-87eb4d6b481f","stem":"The main support of the uterus is provided by","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Obstetrics and Gynecology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The round ligament"},{"label":"B","text":"The cardinal ligament"},{"label":"C","text":"The infandilo-pelvic ligament"},{"label":"D","text":"The integrity of the pelvis"},{"label":"E","text":"The broad ligament"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Obstetrics and Gynecology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-a847cf66292f","stem":"The most important muscle in the pelvic floor is","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Head and Neck","topicOriginal":"Head and Neck","subtopic":"Ear","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Bulbo cavernousus."},{"label":"B","text":"Ischio-cavernosus."},{"label":"C","text":"Levator ani."},{"label":"D","text":"Superficial transverse Perineal muscle."},{"label":"E","text":"Deep transverse Perineal muscle."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Head and Neck","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-4463934199ee","stem":"Which group of bones collectively forms the bony pelvis?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Head and Neck","topicOriginal":"Head and Neck","subtopic":"Ear","suggestedTopic":"Bony pelvis","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Trochanter, hip socket, ischium, sacrum & pubis."},{"label":"B","text":"Ilium, ischium, pubis, sacrum & coccyx."},{"label":"C","text":"Ilium, ischium & pubis."},{"label":"D","text":"Sacrum, Ischium, ilium & pubis."},{"label":"E","text":"Trochanter, sacrum, coccyx, ilium & pubis."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Head and Neck","answerAuditStatus":"independent_checked","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"checked_explained","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[],"manualEdits":[{"field":"stem","original":"The pelvis includes which of the following bones","corrected":"Which group of bones collectively forms the bony pelvis?","reason":"language_or_captured_footer_repair"}]},{"id":"q-daa07149f566","stem":"The joint between the two pubic bones is called the","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Head and Neck","topicOriginal":"Head and Neck","subtopic":"Ear","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Sacroiliac joint."},{"label":"B","text":"Pubis symphysis."},{"label":"C","text":"Sacrococcygeal joint."},{"label":"D","text":"Piriformis."},{"label":"E","text":"Intervertebral joint"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Head and Neck","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-9310fe9c09d7","stem":"The greatest diameter of the fetal head is","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Embryology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Occipitofrontal."},{"label":"B","text":"Occipitomental."},{"label":"C","text":"Suboccipit bregmatic. 6 All OB-GYN MCQs Second rearranged Edition 2011"},{"label":"D","text":"Bitemporal."},{"label":"E","text":"Biparietal."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Embryology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-4b741475947a","stem":"Molding of the fetal head","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Embryology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Usually cause brain damage."},{"label":"B","text":"Becomes progressively easier as gestational age increase."},{"label":"C","text":"Increase the difficulty of delivery."},{"label":"D","text":"Does NOT have time to occur in breech delivery."},{"label":"E","text":"Does not happen when maternal pelvis is adequate."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Embryology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-26c5403c71f4","stem":"The main blood supply of the vulva is","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Inferior hemorrhoidal artery."},{"label":"B","text":"Pudendal artery."},{"label":"C","text":"Ilioinguinal artery."},{"label":"D","text":"Femoral artery."},{"label":"E","text":"Inferior Hypogastric artery."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-5c086fb7a239","stem":"The following are typical in the female bony pelvis EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Head and Neck","topicOriginal":"Head and Neck","subtopic":"Ear","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Has a transverse diameter of the inlet greater than the antero-posterior diameter."},{"label":"B","text":"Has an obstetric conjugate of 11-12 cm."},{"label":"C","text":"Is funnel shaped."},{"label":"D","text":"Has an obtuse greater sciatic notch."},{"label":"E","text":"Has a pubic angle greater than 90 degrees."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Head and Neck","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-b022220d88a9","stem":"Regarding fetal head, Choose the CORRECT answer","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Embryology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Can be delivered vaginally in persistent occipito-mental Presentation."},{"label":"B","text":"Will show Spalding's sign within 12 hours of Intrauterine death."},{"label":"C","text":"Can be delivered vaginally in persistent brow presentation."},{"label":"D","text":"Is likely to be a vertex presentation when the head is deflexed."},{"label":"E","text":"Considered to be engaged when the Biparietal diameter passes the level of the pelvic inlet."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Embryology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["answer_explanation_mixed_into_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-cd1c3a940746","stem":"The ovarian artery usually arises from which vessel?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Head and Neck","topicOriginal":"Head and Neck","subtopic":"Ear","suggestedTopic":"Female pelvic blood supply","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Common iliac artery."},{"label":"B","text":"Internal iliac artery."},{"label":"C","text":"Aorta."},{"label":"D","text":"Hypogastric artery."},{"label":"E","text":"Sacral artery."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Head and Neck","answerAuditStatus":"independent_checked","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"checked_explained","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[],"manualEdits":[{"field":"stem","original":"The ovarian artery is a branch of","corrected":"The ovarian artery usually arises from which vessel?","reason":"language_or_captured_footer_repair"}]},{"id":"q-1b5317d681ff","stem":"The normal lining of the fallopian tube is","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Squamous epithelium."},{"label":"B","text":"Transitional epithelium."},{"label":"C","text":"Cuboidal epithelium. 7 All OB-GYN MCQs Second rearranged Edition 2011"},{"label":"D","text":"Columnar epithelium with cilia."},{"label":"E","text":"Fibrous connective tissue."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-c21879fe828d","stem":"The cilia of the fallopian tube has the following function","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Remove the zona pellucida which surrounds the ovum."},{"label":"B","text":"Transport the ovum towards the uterus."},{"label":"C","text":"Enhance the rapid division of the zygote."},{"label":"D","text":"Transport the ovum towards the peritoneal cavity."},{"label":"E","text":"Has a bactericidal function to prevent peritoneal function 8 All OB-GYN MCQs Second rearranged Edition 2011 Labor and Fetal Surveillance and Mechanism of Labor:"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-aa83c635224a","stem":"Hyperextension of the fetal head is found in","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Embryology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Vertex presentation"},{"label":"B","text":"Face presentation"},{"label":"C","text":"Shoulder presentation"},{"label":"D","text":"Breach presentation"},{"label":"E","text":"Hydrocephalic baby"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Embryology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-2d622c7b9d35","stem":"Stages of labor","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Obstetrics and Gynecology","topic":"Labor and Delivery · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Labor and Delivery","options":[{"label":"A","text":"The first stage commences at the time of membrane rupture"},{"label":"B","text":"The cervix dilates at consistent rate of 3 cm per hour in the first stage"},{"label":"C","text":"The third stage end with the delivery of the placenta and membranes"},{"label":"D","text":"Forceps or ventose may be useful in slow progress of the late 1st stage"},{"label":"E","text":"Syntometrine is a combination of oxytocin and Ergometrine which is used in the treatment of secondary postpartum haemorrhage (PPH)"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Obstetrics and Gynecology","displayTopic":"Labor and Delivery · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-35af8f5e893d","stem":"All the following characteristics are applied to a pelvis favorable to vaginal delivery EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Head and Neck","topicOriginal":"Head and Neck","subtopic":"Ear","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Sacral promontory can not be felt."},{"label":"B","text":"Obstetric conjugate is less than 10 cm."},{"label":"C","text":"Ischial spines are not prominent."},{"label":"D","text":"Subpubic arch accepts 2 fingers."},{"label":"E","text":"Intertuberous diameter accepts 4 knuckles on pelvic exam."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Head and Neck","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-bcacf77e5b54","stem":"In the fetus","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The coronal suture lies between the two parietal bones."},{"label":"B","text":"The umbilical artery normally contains one artery and two veins."},{"label":"C","text":"Fetal lie describes the long axis of the fetus to the long axis of the mother."},{"label":"D","text":"Entanglement of the umbilical cord is common in diamniotic twins."},{"label":"E","text":"The anterior Fontanelle is usually closed by the time of labor."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["short_or_incomplete_stem","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["short_or_incomp