causes all of the following EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Spontaneous abortions."},{"label":"B","text":"Premature labor."},{"label":"C","text":"Pregnancy induced hypertension."},{"label":"D","text":"Abnormal fetal lie."},{"label":"E","text":"May Obstruct labor. 20 All OB-GYN MCQs Second rearranged Edition 2011"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-155a59863dae","stem":"Ovarian Dysgenesis is associated with the elevation of which of the following hormones.","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Pituitary Gonadotropins."},{"label":"B","text":"Estradiol."},{"label":"C","text":"Estriol."},{"label":"D","text":"Pregnandiol."},{"label":"E","text":"Progesterone."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-b16c34eca445","stem":"Confirmation of the diagnosis of Turner syndrome is best done by","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Gyn PV examination."},{"label":"B","text":"Pregnantriol estimation."},{"label":"C","text":"Hysterosalpingography (HSG)"},{"label":"D","text":"Chromosomal analysis (Karyotyping)."},{"label":"E","text":"Estimation of hypophyseal gonadotropins."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-23e2e2c366ac","stem":"In cases of androgen insensitivity syndrome the following findings are true EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The chromosomal sex is 46 XX"},{"label":"B","text":"Scant or no pubic or axillary hair."},{"label":"C","text":"No uterus."},{"label":"D","text":"Normal female external genitalia."},{"label":"E","text":"Breast are usually well developed."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-d2e64d33fc32","stem":"In testicular feminization syndrome","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"There are usually normal testes."},{"label":"B","text":"Kalman's syndrome is a recognized cause."},{"label":"C","text":"Breast development is usually lacking."},{"label":"D","text":"There's usually very low testosterone level."},{"label":"E","text":"The karyotype is 46 XX."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-dc63cf5ac189","stem":"In Turner's syndrome, the following are usually observed EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The ovaries are usually well developed."},{"label":"B","text":"The nipples are widely spaced."},{"label":"C","text":"The girl is of short stature."},{"label":"D","text":"Has a webbed neck."},{"label":"E","text":"The condition can be diagnosed by chromosomal analysis."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-8645fba11dd4","stem":"Regarding the Development of internal genital organs","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The uterus, fallopian tubes, cervix & upper vagina develop from the mesophrenic duct."},{"label":"B","text":"The testes secretes testosterone which cause regression of the müllerian ducts in the male fetus."},{"label":"C","text":"The vagina is formed by the Urogenital sinus. 21 All OB-GYN MCQs Second rearranged Edition 2011"},{"label":"D","text":"Müllerian agenesis (Mayer- Rokittanky - Kuster - Huser syndromes) is characterized by the absence of the uterus & upper vagina with normal female external genetailia & 46 XX."},{"label":"E","text":"Bicornuate uterus & uterus didelphus result from vertical fusion defects of the müllerian ducts."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-67f84a15fa01","stem":"Regarding puberty, all of the following are true EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is the transitional period of development during which an individual matures from childhood to sexual & reproductive maturity."},{"label":"B","text":"Breast budding is the 1ST visible sign of puberty."},{"label":"C","text":"The maximum growth velocity occurs at 12 years."},{"label":"D","text":"The age of menarche has decreased over the last 3-4 decades due to improved nutrition, general health & lifestyle changes."},{"label":"E","text":"Thelarche marks the attainment of reproductive maturity."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-6de10e535e40","stem":"Turner's syndrome is associated with","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Absent uterus"},{"label":"B","text":"Normal breast development"},{"label":"C","text":"Primary amenorrhea"},{"label":"D","text":"Hirsutism"},{"label":"E","text":"Normal height"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-843d2e83e8c2","stem":"Anomalies or the uterus can be associated with the following EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Obstetrics and Gynecology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Urinary tract abnormalities."},{"label":"B","text":"Recurrent pregnancies loss."},{"label":"C","text":"Preterm labor."},{"label":"D","text":"Müllerian tract anomalies."},{"label":"F","text":"Polycystic ovary."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Obstetrics and Gynecology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-3acb1cf8f45f","stem":"First endocrine influence in 2ry sexual characters","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Secretion of delta-4 Androstenedione from the adrenal gland"},{"label":"B","text":"Pineal body maturation"},{"label":"C","text":"Pituitary maturation"},{"label":"D","text":"Hypothalamic down regulation."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-388cfa898c8e","stem":"Follicular growth (in 