tem":"Spinnbarkheit is a term which means","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Crystallization of the cervical mucous."},{"label":"B","text":"Thickening of the cervical mucous."},{"label":"C","text":"Mucous secretion of the cervix."},{"label":"D","text":"Threading of the cervical mucous."},{"label":"E","text":"Thinning of the cervical mucous."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-a743a8fcc6fd","stem":"Regarding Placental function","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Embryology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"hCG is a glycoprotein composed of alpha & β subunits. It's secreted by cytotrophoblast."},{"label":"B","text":"Human placenta lactogen enhances insulin action & improves glucose tolerance."},{"label":"C","text":"Placental Corticotropin releasing hormone increases ACTH & cortisol & causes vasoconstriction of the feto-placental blood vessels."},{"label":"D","text":"Estrogen is secreted by the feto-placental unit responsible for the growth of the myometrium & angiogenesis."},{"label":"E","text":"Progesterone causes vasodilatation of blood vessels & contraction of uterine smooth muscle."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Embryology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-b554e35d380b","stem":"Regarding placental anatomy","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Human Anatomy","topic":"Head and Neck","topicOriginal":"Head and Neck","subtopic":"Ear","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The decidua capsularis forms part of the placenta."},{"label":"B","text":"The fetal side of the placenta is divided into 30-40 cotyledons."},{"label":"C","text":"The intervillous space contains fetal blood."},{"label":"D","text":"Anatomically the placenta id fully formed by 30 weeks."},{"label":"E","text":"Fetal blood vessels develop in the mesenchymal core of the chorionic villi."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Head and Neck","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-ca598c6c5d9e","stem":"Which of the following does NOT accurately describes the placenta in humans","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Embryology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"15-20 cm in diameter."},{"label":"B","text":"2-4 cm thick."},{"label":"C","text":"Weighs about 1/6 of what the term infant does."},{"label":"D","text":"Delivered from maternal & fetal tissue."},{"label":"E","text":"Umbilical cord originates from the center of the placenta in all most of the cases."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Embryology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-78485c48422e","stem":"Maternal serum Prolactin levels in pregnancy are highest","ty