ension of the fetal head is a favorable"},{"label":"C","text":"External cephalic version (ECV), reduces the breech presentation at term 1%"},{"label":"D","text":"Mid trimester amniocentesis is likely to result in breech presentation at term"},{"label":"E","text":"The perinatal morbidity is ten time higher than in cephalic presentation"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-2008e2ed9d91","stem":"External cephalic version is contraindicated in all of these conditions EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Scarred uterus"},{"label":"B","text":"Multiple pregnancy"},{"label":"C","text":"Placenta previa"},{"label":"D","text":"Severe maternal hypertension"},{"label":"E","text":"Gestational diabetes 100 All OB-GYN MCQs Second rearranged Edition 2011"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-5c49644889b9","stem":"Regarding Breech presentation, the following are true EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Accounts for up to 3 % term pregnancies"},{"label":"B","text":"May be diagnosed on clinical examination of the abdomen"},{"labe