 133 All OB-GYN MCQs Second rearranged Edition 2011"},{"label":"C","text":"There is a substantial risk in older women with venous thrombus & embolism in their user."},{"label":"D","text":"Breakthrough bleeding is rare."},{"label":"E","text":"The dose of progesterone is much larger than in combined."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["answer_explanation_mixed_into_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-17c90206c55b","stem":"The goals for developing a successful contraceptive include all of the following EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Regulating fertility."},{"label":"B","text":"Stabilizing population."},{"label":"C","text":"Reducing maternal morbidity."},{"label":"D","text":"Diminishing the incidence."},{"label":"E","text":"Decreasing the prevalence of sexually transmitted diseases."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-7cdac6a72176","stem":"Regarding IUCD, all of the following are INCORRECT, EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Inhibition of ovulation is the main mechanism of action."},{"label":"B","text":"Has a failure of 6%."},{"label":"C","text":"Statistically increases the incidence of ectopic pregnancy."},{"label":"D","text":"Is commonly associated with excessive menstrual loss."},{"label":"E","text":"Not suitable for patients with previous delivery."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-be26a220592d","stem":"The following are known contraindications to the use of combined oral contraceptive pills (COCP), EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Endocrine Pharmacology · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Endocrine Pharmacology","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Deep venous thrombosis or pulmonary embolism."},{"label":"B","text":"Active liver disease."},{"label":"C","text":"Benign intracranial hypertension."},{"label":"D","text":"Repeated LSCS."},{"label":"E","text":"Cholestasis in pregnancy."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Endocrine Pharmacology · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-8794da7dcb3b","stem":"The combined oral contraceptive pill, besides being used as a method of contraception, can be used to treat the following, EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Endometriosis."},{"label":"B","text":"Ovulation pain."},{"label":"C","text":"Menorrhagia."},{"label":"D","text":"Dysmenorrhea."},{"label":"E","text"