clude all of the following EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Genital atrophy 150 All OB-GYN MCQs Second rearranged Edition 2011"},{"label":"B","text":"Feeling of lethargy"},{"label":"C","text":"Complete lactation failure"},{"label":"D","text":"Amenorrhea"},{"label":"E","text":"Increased basal metabolic rate"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-521825e7ed0d","stem":"A 48-year-woman who had two normal pregnancies 13 and 15 years ago presents with the complaint of amenorrhea for 7 months. She expresses the desire to become pregnant again. After exclusion of pregnancy, which of the following tests is next indicated in the evaluation of this patient's amenorrhea?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Obstetrics and Gynecology","topic":"Antenatal Care · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Antenatal Care","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Hysterosalpingogram."},{"label":"B","text":"Endometrial biopsy."},{"label":"C","text":"Thyroid function test."},{"label":"D","text":"Testosterone and DHAS levels."},{"label":"E","text":"LH and FSH levels."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Obstetrics and Gynecology","displayTopic":"Antenatal Care · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-64d4cd7ad2bd","stem":"In 