st Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Bromocriptine use."},{"label":"B","text":"Excess glucocorticosteroid usage."},{"label":"C","text":"Androgen excess in the female."},{"label":"D","text":"Early menarche."},{"label":"E","text":"Excessive protein intake."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-0edb2fbe76ed","stem":"The use of estrogen alone in menopausal women increase the risk of","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Endometrial cancer"},{"label":"B","text":"Ovarian cancer"},{"label":"C","text":"Bone cancer"},{"label":"D","text":"Bowel cancer"},{"label":"E","text":"All of the above"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-c97fc9b74fe3","stem":"Recently the main risk of hormone replacement therapy after menopause is","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"fracture the neck of femur"},{"label":"B","text":"Cancer of the colon"},{"label":"C","text":"Hirsutism"},{"label":"D","text":"Cancer of breast"},{"label":"E","text":"Genital atrophy"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-9f9e460d9a05","stem":"In the menopause","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Osteoporosis is common in black women"},{"label":"B","text":"They have increase tendency of fracture"},{"label":"C","text":"Post menopausal bleeding is always due to endometrial carcinoma"},{"label":"D","text":"HRT is always indicated"},{"label":"E","text":"OCP can be used as hormone replacement"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-ca3a065a435e","stem":"Postmenopausal women","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Malignancy is the commonest cause of postmenopausal bleeding."},{"label":"B","text":"FSH and LH are characteristically low."},{"label":"C","text":"Fibroid uterus tends to grow bigger."},{"label":"D","text":"Hormonal replacement therapy increases the risk of breast cancer."},{"label":"E","text":"Endometrium is characteristically thick on USS."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-d2dee61073cf","stem":"Which of the following is an indication for estrogen treatment?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Fibroid."},{"label":"B","text":"Threatened abortion."},{"label":"C","text":"Endometriosis."},{"label":"D","text":"Postmenopausal atrophic vaginitis. 158 All OB-GYN MCQs Second rearranged Edition 2011"},{"label":"E","text":"Induction of ovulation for anovulatory cycle."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-8e49b839a382","stem":"The following is a symptom of Climacteric(menopause)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"obesity."},{"label":"B","text":"Premenstrual tension."},{"label":"C","text":"Hot flushes."},{"label":"D","text":"Menorrhagia."},{"label":"E","text":"Ectopic pregnancy"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-784d036e512a","stem":"Regarding hot flushes in the menopausal period. All the following are true, EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"They are reduced by exercise."},{"label":"B","text":"They are less in obese women."},{"label":"C","text":"They are more in smoking women."},{"label":"D","text":"The best treatment is HRT."},{"label":"E","text":"It usually disappears in 1 month."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-2aefd7c2b1c8","stem":"Which of the following statement is INCORRECT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Climacteric is the phase during which a woman passes form the reproductive stage to non-reproductive stage."},{"label":"B","text":"Pre-menopause is the time during climacteric during which the periods becomes irregular."},{"label":"C","text":"Menopause is the final menstruation which occurs during the climacteric."},{"label":"D","text":"Premature menopause is cessation of menstruation before the age of 40."},{"label":"E","text":"Oral contraceptive pills delay the onset of menopause."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-f1fd2a2ddcc3","stem":"True statement concerning the development of postmenopausal osteoporosis include","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"opti